														</div>
			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-4839956">
									

<p>Seeking Greenlights: Yes.</p>
<p>Page Type: SCP Article.</p>
<p>Genre: My design is meant to be spooky, but I may not achieve this factor.</p>
<p>Page Layout: The usual SCP statements, Item Name, Item Class but no picture. Information is going to be structured in the following layout; Appearance description (Height, weight, colour and shape), Discovery (How the anomaly was contained), Abilities (What the anomaly can do, how it does it etc) and the Addendums (Stories about previously explained things).</p>
<p>Elevator Pitch: The basic premise is a tall, slender, arctic hunter with elongated shoulder growths and large elbows, glowing crimson eyes, capable of seeing infrared radiation and heat signature, used for hunting. The anomaly has thousands of tiny muscles on its skin capable of moving guanine crystals to adjust the wavelength of light being reflected off the skin of the anomaly. This is commonly known as camouflage, and is the same method that the Chamaeleonidae (Common Chameleon) uses. Bone marrow scans and nervous axon scans have suggested that overgrowths on the anomaly's shoulder blades and elbows contain many nerve endings, which transfer electrical signals in large amounts to a particular area which creates an electromagnetic field. These electromagnetic pulses disrupt nearby local electric signals. It may use this to alter the function of electrical signals in the brain, or to inhibit power of technology.</p>
<p>Central Narrative: It was a normal day in the UK Arctic Research Facility. It was collection day, where the scientific staff would take a collection of snow for carbon-testing, a process where the amount of carbon that is in a snowflake is collected. Suddenly, the power went out. As the staff stumbled over to the generator, senior researcher Noel Leon noticed a small red glow. Must have been nothing. He got back to fixing the generator and replaced the fuses. But as soon as the generator start-up was initiated, the generator failed. What was going on? Suddenly, pat… pat… pat…. He turned around, but there was nothing but footprints. SNAP. The crunch of his bones in SCP-XXXX's mouth was horrifying, but unheard to remaining staff. As it entered the facility, seven of it's prey had already been frozen. An easy meal. Junior researcher Doctor Edward turned a corner, but the anomaly was gone, just a frozen, half-eaten corpse. He was petrified, and sprinted out to the door and locked it shut. His frozen fingers dialled 911 into a telephone. The rest of the facility was wiped out, with the exception of Doctor Bradly who was obliterated by SCP-XXXX. Doctor Bradly called local authorities and the foundation was alerted. MTF unit Delta-92 Snow-and-Tell was sent to the situation immediately. Using infrared vision, the anomaly's ability was stunted, rendering it useless. Using a Class-3 collapsible containment cell, SCP-XXXX was taken to Site-25 via helicopter with ease.</p>

